# Save over the existing slot 1, so the save directory keeps exactly one
# save. Creating a second one would make lib/restore_slot1.xit ambiguous
# (both rows would read "ZZZZ"), and renaming files behind the game's back
# is the kind of shortcut that works until it silently does not.
#
# Same menu geometry as save_as_ZZZZ.xit; the difference is clicking the
# existing row at (100,78) instead of typing a fresh name.

move 35 174
run 10
click left
run 40
move 160 56
run 10
click left
run 50
move 100 78
run 10
click left
run 30
move 65 168
run 10
click left
run 70

# "Overwrite the saved game?" -- Yes at (157,95), No at (157,111), measured
# from the rendered box. Without this the dialogue stays up and the save is
# never written, which is visible only as a save file whose mtime never
# changed.
move 157 95
run 10
click left
run 70
move 305 196
run 15
